 "summary": "The ACS and stable-angina rules (and the character check_for) leave out two of the page's five ACS features, \"not relieved by rest or sublingual nitrates\" and \"occurs more often than usual\". As a result, a known stable-angina patient with crescendo or nitrate-resistant pain is diagnosed as stable angina, not ACS. Smaller issues: \"minimal effort\" is dropped from \"occurs at rest\", \"than usual\" is lost in the Worsening/Prolonged qualifiers, and \"lasts ≥ 10 minutes\" is approximated by onset time with an overlapping <= boundary. In the red box, \"Chest discomfort\" + New has no site."
}